					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-4316360</guid>
				<title>Ethics Committee FTW</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-4316360</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 27 Jul 2019 23:20:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Vermillion Fenrir</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1747245</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>From now on, I will forever look up to the Ethics Committee as the MVP of the Foundation.</p> <p>A &quot;Lawful Good&quot; side of a Foundation that fashion itself right from the very front as &quot;Lawful Evil&quot; which seen as a joke the entire time, but truthfully, hold enough power to advise the 05 themselves.</p> <p>And I absolutely adore the strict and stern tone. It is like they knew that there's &quot;evil&quot; thing that they cannot just let go, and they will do all things necessary to makes sure that the Foundation will continue to do its work, however without abandoning morality and humanity.</p> <p>They're the hidden force that enforce the said law, in a world where we think, there's no &quot;morality&quot; within such cruel and cold Foundation. Then you see the light, AND that light is not soft nor weak. That light is blunt, harsh, severe and strong. Enough to illuminate the dark, and cut down the vile.</p> <p>Never seen I'll say this&#8230;. but apparently, heroes exist in here too, on the Foundation.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I will proudly join the Ethics Committee if they're real hahaha</span></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
