					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2081656</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2081656</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 05 Aug 2014 14:56:53 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Ndf</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1945587</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>What Zyn said. The Foundation is not the GOC, they're goals are not to destroy or control paranormal/supernatural phenomenon, it's to conceal it in the interest of &quot;normality&quot;. To quote: &quot;While the rest of mankind dwells in the light, we must stand in the darkness to fight it, contain it, and shield it from the eyes of the public, so that others may live in a sane and normal world.&quot;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2077414</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2077414</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 29 Jul 2014 07:50:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>turquoise</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1939510</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I may be wrong here, but I think the idea is that the scientist is vomiting at the thought that, having been appointed to the committee, he or she will now have to know what procedure 110-Montauk is. Sorry if this constitutes a necropost.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2051388</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2051388</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Jun 2014 21:14:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The general population doesn't have to know about the Foundation for the Foundation to protect it.</p> <p>Basically, it's supposed to read like &quot;The general population might <em>think</em> it wants to be informed about everything, but the Foundation keeps them in the dark in their best interests, since they wouldn't be able to cope if they knew what we knew.&quot;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2051358</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2051358</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Jun 2014 20:24:21 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Tiktaalik</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1908077</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>110-Montauk was devised using knowledge acquired from a notebooks that belonged to the cultists, its on SCP-231’s page. “based on notebooks recovered from the cult, instituted Procedure 110-Montauk to prevent future occurrences”.</p> <p>The Ethics Committee designed Procedure 110-Montauk using information from the cult's note books.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2051353</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2051353</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Jun 2014 20:15:48 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Tiktaalik</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1908077</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The only thing I didn’t like about this was the “Regardless of what the general population might think it wants, what we do, what the Foundation does, is in the overall best interests of that general population.” I was under the impression the foundation was a SECRET organization. Thus the general population doesn’t know about it, and thus wouldn’t suspect it does anything, including exist, except maybe a few conspiracy theorists that pretty much no-one takes seriously. Groups of intrest are of course outside of the general population. That aside this tale was spectacular. +1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-2036677</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-2036677</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 22 May 2014 03:01:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Koekr8144</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1649893</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Intelligent and influential.<br /> Just one problem with it though.<br /> Why would a foundation scientist shake at the thought of deciding when cruelty is necessary and vomit at the thought of someone having to create procedure 110 montauk? It seems too petty for someone who already knows a thousand more terrible ways to die than a psychotic murderer with a creative knack.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236#post-1935108</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403236/ethics-committee-orientation#post-1935108</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 13 Jan 2014 19:27:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dr Reach</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1779895</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The fact that the Ethics Committee is both so influential and so straight in their duties makes you realize that, whatever the Foundation does, there is always something <em>worse</em> if they don't do it.</p> <p><sub>It is called <em>choosing the lesser evil</em>, and has real applications in the real world. Now wonder what lesser evils are being perpetrated right now, in our world, in our very real, very difficult world.</sub></p> <p><sub>Just a piece of my mind.</sub></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
